# E §5 step 1, L §4.4 A movement takes a day (tally 2.3, #247; C-4's clause on a window's hole day; 2.2.1's
# n4_20260320): the window reaches pay's `on`, so pay is a hole day, and a binding over `adjustments` that could hold
# the adjustment a1 makes is the hole naming w. Before: 0, or a count read per day of the window.
=== m.tally
model bk20260320
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input w: date
input d_at: date
move pay: transfers
  on w
  at d_at
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d_at = 2026-03-01 "s"
  w = window(2026-03-03, 2026-03-25) "s"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
version a0
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
version a1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-20
  replace amt = 150.00 PLN "s"
ask adj: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04)
=== expect
adj: ?"date within window(2026-03-03, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of pay" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-06-10
